---
title: Chocolate Peppermint Kiss Cookies
servings: 40
cuisine: american
main_protein: none
prep_time: "12 minutes"
cook_time: "8 minutes"
tags:
  - dessert
  - chocolate
  - peppermint
  - cookie
  - christmas
  - baking
image: ../obsidian/attachments/Pasted image 20240116181103.png
leftover_portions: 36
prep:
  - Preheat oven to 350°F
  - Line baking sheets with parchment paper
  - Soften 1 cup butter
  - Unwrap the candy cane kisses
---
Preheat #oven{} to 350°F. Prepare #baking sheets{} by lining with parchment paper or silicone sheets.

In a medium bowl, whisk together @all-purpose flour{2%cups}, @unsweetened cocoa powder{0.33%cup} and @fine salt{0.25%tsp}.

Using an #electric mixer{} and a large bowl (or a stand mixer), beat @unsalted butter{1%cup}, softened, and 1 cup of the @sugar{1.5%cups} on medium-high until light and fluffy (about ~{3%minutes}). Add @egg{1} and @pure vanilla extract{1%tbsp} and beat until combined. Turn mixer to low and gradually add flour mixture until combined.

Put the remaining 1/2 cup of sugar in a small bowl. Form dough into approximately 1-inch balls and then roll in sugar to coat. Place one inch apart on prepared baking sheets.

Bake for ~{8%minutes} or until cookies are set but still look moist. Remove from the oven and lightly press @candy cane kisses{10%oz} into the center of each cookie.

Cool completely on the cookie sheets on wire racks before removing to an airtight container to store.

-- Each 10 oz. bag of candy kisses contains 70-75 kisses (so you'll have extra to eat!).
-- Our tip: add peppermint extract next time.
